SCOPE OF THE PUBLIC DOMAIN DEDICATION

The dedication in UNLICENSE covers the original content of this pack component: the packwiz
manifest (pack.toml, index.toml, mods/*.pw.toml), the configuration files under config/,
the FTB Quests chapters and lang data, the CI workflows and the documentation.

IT DOES NOT COVER THE MODS.

This source tree contains **no mod jars**. Every one of the ~490 mods in this pack is
downloaded at install time from its original host — Modrinth, CurseForge, or the mod's own
GitHub Release — and each remains under the licence its own author chose. Those licences
range from permissive to all-rights-reserved. Nothing here grants you any right to any of
them.

If you fork or redistribute the source tree, you are redistributing a *list of
references*, not the mods themselves. Published client archives are the exception
described below.

BUILT ARTEFACTS

- The **server pack** published on the Releases page ships the manifest and an installer.
  It contains no mod jars; the installer fetches each mod from its original host on first
  run.

- The **client `.mrpack`** references Modrinth-hosted mods by URL, but the Modrinth pack
  format has no URL mechanism for mods hosted elsewhere, so mods from CurseForge and from
  GitHub Releases are embedded in the archive's `overrides/` directory. That *is*
  redistribution. The exporter prints the exact list of embedded jars in its step log on
  every build. Check that list against those mods' terms before publishing a release more
  widely than the GitHub Releases page.

BERTIE'S OWN MODS

The mods written for this pack live under `mods/` in the Bertie monorepo and released
versions are consumed here as tagged GitHub Releases. Most are dedicated to the public
domain under The Unlicense; one is not:

- `explosive-enhancement` is MIT, being a port of Superkat32's MIT original.

Each mod component carries its own NOTICE with the detail, including individual
assets that are credited to other authors and excluded from the dedication.
